rchived","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":283518839,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyODM1MTg4Mzk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","color":"ffddff","default":true,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1732720779,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxNzMyNzIwNzc5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:gui","name":"topic:gui","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-01-22T12:02:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-24T10:36:36Z","closed_at":"2026-01-24T06:45:04Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6rc2 and before.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.rc2 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.7628) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12490F (12 threads) - 31.81 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n~~**Latest Edit: I have discovered a new issue again, and it seems that I have not noticed the difference between `Never` and `Control Supports Keyboard Input` options. It seems that their functions are the SAME, as both options can display the focus through the keyboard, while the mouse does not.**~~\n\n~~1. `- Control Supports Keyboard Input (1) shows the focused state even when gained via mouse/touch input (similar to how browsers handle focus).` This sentence is difficult to read and understand, and its semantics should also be incorrect.~~\n\n2. Besides, those different enumerations' descriptions format is also different, which also causes chaos. Here are some screenshots:\n\n<img width=\"1453\" height=\"971\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/28b6de45-5721-47b7-963a-4a909f76d777\" />\n\n<img width=\"1467\" height=\"438\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/29c18bad-6018-4344-8e8e-96c2a7fdb998\" />\n\n<img width=\"781\" height=\"512\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d7042dc8-d5af-4a63-82e3-ab7c5d908047\" />\n\nOther situations in the document, but not in EditorSettings:\n\n<img width=\"1321\" height=\"429\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9042769b-b3af-441c-838c-4ce327d29dd2\" />\n\nSome of them include the meaning of enumeration names in the sentence, while others do not. Besides, their formats are also different. In my opinion, the description format of `display/window/stretch/mode` is the most clear.\n\nSorry, it seems that I raised two different issues in one issue. The main issue is still related to the description of the setting in version 4.6. Another issue regarding the description format in the editor, I think it would be more appropriate to leave it for later to unify and improve it (due to the large workload). Therefore, this issue mainly focuses on this option itself.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"MadeScientist","id":190612698,"node_id":"U_kgDOC1yE2g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/190612698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist","html_url":"https://github.com/MadeScientist","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MadeScientist/followers","following_url":"https://api.git